---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

// Textul de mai jos descrie exact ce face codul (api/contact.ts, lib/analytics.ts,
// lib/vitals.ts, harta Google din index.astro). Daca se schimba fluxul de date,
// se schimba si pagina asta, impreuna cu data de mai jos.
const effectiveDate = 'September 2, 2026';

const h2 = 'font-display font-semibold text-2xl text-fg pt-4';
const h3 = 'font-display font-semibold text-xl text-fg pt-1';
const list = 'list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 marker:text-accent-display';
const link =
  'text-accent-on-light font-medium underline underline-offset-4 decoration-1 hover:text-fg transition-colors';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Essential Flooring"
  description="What Essential Flooring Inc collects through this website, who handles it on our behalf, how long it is kept, and how to ask for a copy or deletion."
  noindex
>
  <section class="pt-10 pb-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]} />
      <h1 class="mt-8 font-display font-semibold text-4xl leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-fg">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[14px] text-fg-muted">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed text-fg-body">
        <p>
          This website is operated by {SITE.legalName}, a licensed flooring contractor in
          Sacramento, California ({SITE.license}). This page explains what the site collects,
          why, who handles it on our behalf, and how to ask us to show, correct or delete it.
          We collect the minimum needed to answer your estimate request.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>The short version</h2>
        <ul class={list}>
          <li>We collect what you type into the estimate form, and nothing else about you personally.</li>
          <li>The site sets no cookies. The one exception is the map on our home page, which is served by Google.</li>
          <li>We never sell your information or pass it to advertisers.</li>
          <li>Email or call us and we will show you what we have, fix it, or delete it.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class={h2}>What we collect and why</h2>

        <h3 class={h3}>Your estimate request</h3>
        <p>
          When you send the form on our contact page we receive your name, phone number, email
          address (optional), city, the service you are interested in and whatever you write
          about the project. We use these details only to get back to you, arrange a site visit
          and prepare your quote.
        </p>
        <p>
          The form also records how long it was open before you pressed send, and it contains a
          hidden field that real visitors never see. Both exist only to filter out spam robots
          and tell us nothing about you.
        </p>

        <h3 class={h3}>Your IP address, in hashed form</h3>
        <p>
          To stop one person from flooding the form, our server counts how many requests arrive
          from the same internet connection within ten minutes. It does this with a one-way hash
          (SHA-256 with a secret key) of your IP address, so the stored value cannot be turned
          back into your address. The hash is stored separately from your request. We do not
          store the plain IP address.
        </p>

        <h3 class={h3}>Site measurement, without cookies</h3>
        <p>
          To see which pages people read and how fast the site loads, our own pages send a small
          report to our database: the page address, the domain of the site that linked you here
          (if any), whether you are on a phone, tablet or desktop, and a few speed measurements.
          The report carries a random session number that your browser keeps only until you
          close the tab. It is not a cookie and it is not linked to your name, phone, email or
          IP address. We use no Google Analytics, no advertising pixels and no social media
          tracking.
        </p>

        <h3 class={h3}>Hosting logs</h3>
        <p>
          Like every website, ours runs on servers that keep standard technical logs: the page
          requested, the time, your IP address and browser type. Our hosting provider keeps
          these for security and troubleshooting.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Who handles your information</h2>
        <p>
          We do not share personal information with anyone except the companies that run parts
          of this website for us. They process it only to provide their service to us and may
          not use it for their own purposes.
        </p>
        <ul class={list}>
          <li>
            <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">Supabase</strong> stores our database,
            including estimate requests and the site measurements described above.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">Resend</strong> delivers each estimate request
            to our inbox as an email. If you gave us an email address, it is set as the reply
            address so that our answer goes straight to you.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">Vercel</strong> hosts the website, runs the
            code that receives the form, and keeps the hosting logs described above.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">Google Maps</strong> provides the map of the
            Sacramento area on our home page. It loads only when you scroll near it. Once it
            does, Google receives your IP address and the address of the page you are on, and it
            may set its own cookies. Whether Google uses that to build a picture of you across
            other websites is governed by Google's privacy policy, not ours. We receive nothing
            from it.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Our pages also link to our Instagram, Facebook and Google profiles and offer a WhatsApp
          link for messaging us. Following any of these takes you off our site and onto theirs,
          under their own privacy terms.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>No sale, no advertising</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal information and we do not share it for advertising of any kind.
          Apart from Google's map, no outside party collects information about your activity on
          this site, and we do not allow anyone to track you over time and across other websites.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Estimate requests are kept for as long as we need them to respond to you and as records
          of our business, for example to prepare a quote or refer back to a job we completed. If
          you ask us to delete your request, we remove it from our database and our inbox. Site
          measurements contain no personal information and are kept as statistics.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Your rights and how to use them</h2>
        <p>You can ask us at any time to:</p>
        <ul class={list}>
          <li>tell you what information we hold about you,</li>
          <li>correct something that is wrong,</li>
          <li>delete your request entirely.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class={link}>{SITE.email}</a> or call
          <a href={SITE.phoneHref} class={link}>{SITE.phone}</a>, {SITE.hours}. We may ask you to
          confirm you are the person who sent the request, for example by writing from the same
          email address or calling from the same phone number. There is no charge, and we will
          not treat you any differently for asking.
        </p>
        <p>
          {SITE.legalName} is a small local business and does not meet the size thresholds that
          bring a company under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA, as amended by the
          CPRA). We honor the requests above regardless.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control</h2>
        <p>
          If your browser sends a Do Not Track signal, the page-view and speed measurement
          described above does not run at all. Because we do not sell or share personal
          information and do not track visitors across other websites, there is nothing further
          for a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal to switch off.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This site is for homeowners and property managers and is not directed to anyone under
          16. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a
          child has sent us a request, contact us and we will delete it.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change this policy, the new version is posted on this page with a new effective
          date at the top. We do not keep visitor accounts or a mailing list, so this page is the
          only place changes are announced. Please check it whenever you send us a request.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          {SITE.legalName}, Sacramento, CA, {SITE.license}.
          <br />
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class={link}>{SITE.email}</a>
          <br />
          <a href={SITE.phoneHref} class={link}>{SITE.phone}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
